---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectAtlas from '../../components/ProjectAtlas.astro';
import projects from '../../data/projects';
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects" description="Selected construction engineering experience, interactive essays, case studies, and tools by Austin Woyshnar.">
  <section class="page-intro compact projects-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Projects</span>
    <h1>Engineering experience, grounded in place.</h1>
    <div class="projects-intro-actions">
      <a class="button" href="#project-atlas-heading">Explore the project map <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      <span>{projects.length} projects · Massachusetts, Maine, and Virginia</span>
    </div>
    <p>Construction engineering experience spanning temporary works, shoring and demolition sequencing, erection stability, rigging and crane operations, equipment loads imposed on existing structures, structural field investigations, and contractor-focused design support. Project work includes higher education, aviation, data centers, industrial facilities, healthcare and life-science buildings, commercial properties, and historic structures.</p>
  </section>

  <ProjectAtlas />

  <!-- ============ SECTION 1: SELECTED WORK ============ -->
  <section class="project-grid project-independent" aria-labelledby="independent-projects-heading">
    <div class="log-section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Selected Work</span>
      <h2 id="independent-projects-heading">Research beyond the project site.</h2>
    </div>
    <article class="project-card project-featured">
      <a class="project-visual" href="/writing/the-watershed/"><img src="/writing/the-watershed/assets/scranton-coal-breaker.jpg" alt="Historic coal breaker in Scranton, Pennsylvania" /></a>
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Visual essay · 2026</span><h2><a href="/writing/the-watershed/">The Watershed</a></h2><p>A research-rich, interactive argument about capital flows, regional capability, and industrial succession.</p><ul class="topic-list"><li>Writing</li><li>Data</li><li>Interaction</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/writing/the-watershed/">Open project ↗</a></div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 2: ENGINEERING CASE STUDIES ============
       To add a new entry: copy one <article class="log-entry"> block below,
       paste it at the TOP of the list, and edit the date, title, tags, and text. -->
  <section class="project-grid">
    <div class="log-section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Engineering Case Studies</span>
      <p class="log-section-note">A dated log of construction engineering work. Generic on client and location. Specific on method.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="log-entry">
      <span class="eyebrow">Logged · July 2026</span>
      <h3>Data Center Grating — Equipment Load Analysis</h3>
      <p>Bar grating capacity analysis for scissor- and boom-lift equipment loads during data center fit-out. Governed by concentrated point-load and wheel-load checks against manufacturer grating capacity tables. The controlling constraint was lift loads exceeding uniform-load ratings; resolved by defining allowable equipment travel paths across the deck.</p>
      <ul class="topic-list"><li>Equipment Loads</li><li>Temporary Works</li></ul>
    </article>

    <article class="log-entry log-draft">
      <span class="eyebrow">Draft — replace this entry</span>
      <h3>Case Study Title Goes Here</h3>
      <p>Draft — replace this text. Describe the engineering problem in one sentence, the governing standards or method in one sentence, and how the key constraint was resolved in one or two sentences. Keep the client and location generic.</p>
      <ul class="topic-list"><li>Tag One</li><li>Tag Two</li></ul>
    </article>

    <article class="log-entry log-draft">
      <span class="eyebrow">Draft — replace this entry</span>
      <h3>Case Study Title Goes Here</h3>
      <p>Draft — replace this text. Describe the engineering problem in one sentence, the governing standards or method in one sentence, and how the key constraint was resolved in one or two sentences. Keep the client and location generic.</p>
      <ul class="topic-list"><li>Tag One</li><li>Tag Two</li></ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 3: TOOLS ============
       Display-only showcase cards. No logins, no live tool access. -->
  <section class="project-grid">
    <div class="log-section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Tools</span>
      <p class="log-section-note">Tools I build for my own analysis, shown here as a display shelf. Engineering tools will be added over time.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="project-card tool-card">
      <div class="project-visual tool-visual"><img src="/projects/tool-placeholder.svg" alt="Placeholder — screenshot coming soon" /></div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Personal tool · In use</span>
        <h3>Real Estate Analysis Tools</h3>
        <p>A working set of models for evaluating small residential and commercial acquisitions — purchase, rehab, rental, and refinance assumptions in one place.</p>
        <ul class="topic-list"><li>Real Estate</li><li>Analysis</li></ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
